From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] shared/tinyusb: read the CDC TX space once per write.

Long output over the native USB CDC console now and then carried bytes
from past the end of the string being printed: the line, then NUL bytes
padding it to its heap block, sometimes the next object's header
(micropython-pydevices#163). Seen on an ESP32-S3 (LilyGo T-Embed) and an
ESP32-P4, both on TinyUSB 0.21.

mp_usbd_cdc_tx_strn() limits each write to the space in the TX FIFO with

    n = MIN(n, tud_cdc_write_available());

MIN() is a macro, so tud_cdc_write_available() runs twice: once in the
comparison and again for the result. When the FIFO is nearly full the
first call returns less than what is left of the string, and if the USB
interrupt completes an IN transfer before the second call, that one
returns the larger, freed space. n then exceeds len - i and tud_cdc_write()
copies past the end of str.

A ring recording the loop's state on every pass caught it on the T-Embed:
a 0x2cf-byte string with 0x29f bytes sent asked to write 0x40, with only
0x30 left, while len, str and i were all intact. The second run caught a
0xc0-byte write with 0x84 left.

The space is now read once into a local.

Based-on: micropython b70ae1aca (v1.30.0-preview-160)
---
 shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_cdc.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_cdc.c b/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_cdc.c
index a5f60c8..4a84966 100644
--- a/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_cdc.c
+++ b/shared/tinyusb/mp_usbd_cdc.c
@@ -114,7 +114,12 @@ mp_uint_t mp_usbd_cdc_tx_strn(const char *str, mp_uint_t len) {
             // (If not connected then we write everything to the fifo, expecting
             // it to overwrite old data so it will have latest data buffered
             // when host connects.)
-            n = MIN(n, tud_cdc_write_available());
+            //
+            // Read the space once: MIN() is a macro, and the USB interrupt can
+            // free space between two calls, so the second could return more
+            // than is left of str.
+            uint32_t available = tud_cdc_write_available();
+            n = MIN(n, available);
         }
 
         uint32_t n2 = tud_cdc_write(str + i, n);
-- 
